Phase 2 (FullSpectrum engine emission) prerequisite: declare the
mixed-filament + dithering keys as typed fields in PrintConfig.hpp so
engine code can use typed `cfg.opt<ConfigOptionBool>("dithering_local_z_mode")
->value` without runtime cast failures.

Patch 0016 already added the matching `this->add(...)` registrations
in PrintConfig.cpp so the keys deserialize cleanly via
`set_deserialize_nothrow` (DynamicConfig surface). But the engine
emission patches port FS v0.9.9 code that accesses the same keys via
typed `PrintConfig::dithering_local_z_mode.value` style — that route
needs the field declared in the PRINT_CONFIG_CLASS_DERIVED_DEFINE
macro expansion. Without these declarations the compile fails with
'class Slic3r::PrintConfig has no member named ...'.

The 20 fields here mirror FS v0.9.9
(ratdoux/OrcaSlicer-FullSpectrum@v0.9.9 commit b3c41fda):

  Region-level overrides (PrintRegionConfig):
    - enable_infill_filament_override (coBool)
    - infill_filament_use_base_first_layers (coInt)
    - infill_filament_use_base_last_layers (coInt)

  Print-level dithering + mixed-filament + cadence (PrintConfig):
    - mixed_color_layer_height_a / _b  (coFloat)
    - mixed_filament_gradient_mode (coBool)
    - mixed_filament_height_lower_bound / _upper_bound (coFloat)
    - mixed_filament_advanced_dithering (coBool)
    - mixed_filament_pointillism_pixel_size / _line_gap (coFloat)
    - mixed_filament_component_bias_enabled (coBool)
    - mixed_filament_surface_indentation (coFloat)
    - mixed_filament_region_collapse (coBool)
    - mixed_filament_definitions (coString)
    - dithering_z_step_size (coFloat)
    - dithering_local_z_mode (coBool)
    - dithering_local_z_whole_objects (coBool)
    - dithering_local_z_direct_multicolor (coBool)
    - dithering_step_painted_zones_only (coBool)
    - local_z_wipe_tower_purge_lines (coFloat)

No behavior change — these are dead until the engine emission patches
that consume them land.

